{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027281-sell-me-on-cofd","id":1027281,"title":"Sell me on CofD!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-05T14:09:16-08:00","id":1027281,"title":"Sell me on CofD!","content":"Hi. I have been playing NWod for a while (along with Savage Worlds!). Really enjoy it as a system. Have been a little reluctant to move over to CofD. Two questions:<br /> <br /> 1 What makes CofD better? Specifics please! <br /> 2 How compatible are the two systems. i.e. if I like mostly NWod but also like some systems in CofD how easy is that to use. Are merits and other elements easily transferable or are the differences to great?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T14:14:56-08:00","id":1027287,"title":"","content":"Also, how different is CofD from G-d machine Rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T14:17:38-08:00","id":1027289,"title":"","content":"Now are you curious about the system in general, mortals in particular, or specific gamelines? Because my pitch for each is going to be different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T14:22:52-08:00","id":1027290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027281-sell-me-on-cofd?p=1027289#post1027289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now are you curious about the system in general, mortals in particular, or specific gamelines? Because my pitch for each is going to be different.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gneral/Mortals and Mage. Maybe Werewolf too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T14:24:22-08:00","id":1027292,"title":"","content":"Particularly interested in how interchangable basic elements such as merits are and how easy it is to incorporate elements from CofD into a game run mostly on NWod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T14:28:28-08:00","id":1027295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027281-sell-me-on-cofd?p=1027290#post1027290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Gneral/Mortals and Mage. Maybe Werewolf too!</div> </div> </div> </div>So the two biggest fixes for me are the changes to mechanical progression and the overhaul of Morality. With the former, the most important is that exponential xp costs have been removed (which would've been worth the purchase price, honestly) in favor of flat pricing (i.e. the first and fifth dots of something cost the same), and experience is now awarded in play for good roleplay or things like voluntarily taking Dramatic Failures, which keeps the drama rolling. Morality is now Integrity and rather than having a really weird hierarchy of crimes you custom-build breaking points for individual characters, with the added bonus that there's no more Derangements as a result of falling (so no more &quot;I stole something so now I have a phobia!&quot; or gross linking of criminality to mental illness). It's just a lot of little quality of life changes like those.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is probably the most-improved 2e line, in that the rules are a lot cleaner, the Forsaken are actually a physical threat now, and there's more of a focused theme (The Hunt) than the sometimes rambling thing that 1e suffered from. I'll confess that I'm not the hugest Werewolf fan, but even I can see how much better the new edition is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T14:50:42-08:00","id":1027307,"title":"","content":"CoD is NWOD refined, the best distilled into pure gold<br /> <br /> The experience rules are better, it allows you to be powerful and awesome, but rewards you for being vulnerable and not simply power gaming. <br /> <br /> The Social Rules are really cool. <br /> <br /> The settings are unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T14:59:47-08:00","id":1027312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027281-sell-me-on-cofd?p=1027287#post1027287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, how different is CofD from G-d machine Rules?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Short answer:</b> It's not. The name change is more of a licensed property thing, not specifically meant to delineate editions. Paradox Interactive just didn't want two distinct The Worlds of Darkness potentially competing for mindshare, so one is Chronicles now.<br /> <br /> <b>Longer answer:</b> The Chronicles of Darkness Revised Storytelling System Rulebook, as opposed to combining the World of Darkness Storytelling System Rulebook with the God-Machine Rules Update, adds optional subsystems for investigating mysteries, foot chases, crafting equipment, and for miscellaneous material Horrors like mothmen, shapeshifters, and black-eyed kids. It's got a few new Merits, about half of which tie into the extra subsystems. It omits some of the explanatory fluff to the God-Machine Chronicle conceit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027281-sell-me-on-cofd?p=1027292#post1027292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Particularly interested in how interchangable basic elements such as merits are and how easy it is to incorporate elements from CofD into a game run mostly on NWod.</div> </div> </div> </div>No quite straight answer to this one. Some Merits or powers or whatever plug in effortlessly into the second edition rules, because the system backbone is almost fully intact: same Attributes, same Skills, same roll resolution. Some require tweaking because of altered systems: for example, a Merit that detects people with a specific Virtue or Vice is going to need adjustment, because Virtue and Vice are no longer picked specifically out of set lists, but freely defined. And some risk choking from the rug being pulled out under them: the derangement subsystem is gone, for example, making any Merits dealing with coping with them non-starters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T15:35:14-08:00","id":1027333,"title":"","content":"What abut changes to mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T15:45:49-08:00","id":1027337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027281-sell-me-on-cofd?p=1027333#post1027333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What abut changes to mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>To put matters simple, the magic system has been overhauled in 2E to be far easier to understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T15:46:47-08:00","id":1027338,"title":"","content":"About Mage: You have Gnosis and Arcana and belong to Path and Order. This is the same - rest is changed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Wisdom is about consequences and prudent use of magic, not morality of it. Yantras and Reach remade spellcasting systems - Yantras are general mechanics on various 'spell bonuses', that previously were Magical Tools or High Speech, for example. You now have larger number of them to use, but they expand with Gnosis of Awakened. Reaches let you use more advanced versions of the spell but on the risk of Paradox - the all 1E 'Add 1 Arcanum dot for X'. And Mage Sight and Mage Armor are completely different mechanics. Mages also get Obsessions, that are Mysteries leaded special Aspirations, generating not only XP but also Mana and Willpower. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Mechanic-wise, Awakening 1E and 2E are two completely different games using only basis of Gnosis and Arcana for it as common start. You can transplant ideas between editions - just changes in core spellcasting mechanics make them more like redoing things than just tweaking, most of the time. BUT devs made almost all major mechanics from 11 years of 1E gameline in 2E corebook - like Supernal Summonig or Abyssal Beings are ready for 2E usage. All Left-Handed practice have at least simple rules to run with them. Proximi Dynasties have stable rules. Stuff like that. <br /> <br /> Mage 2E is streamlined, remade whole 1E gameline in one book! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-05-2017, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T16:02:20-08:00","id":1027339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1027281-sell-me-on-cofd?p=1027333#post1027333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What abut changes to mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the big things is that (partially due to the changes to how extended actions work) all spellcasting is cast at ritual length by default; taking more than one interval to cast adds extra dice to the roll, which is notably important since the bulk of enhancements to spells still apply penalties to the roll.<br /> <br /> Another thing is that spell effects are now solidly at the dot rating for their Practice \u2014 no more waiting until Forces 5 to manipulate radiation or needing Space 5 to make a permanent Portal \u2014 but Reach, the resource that goes into using those formerly-limited effects effectively, is made available by having more dots in the Arcanum or by having the spell as a Rote (which allows you to cast with the same Reach as if you had five dots in the Arcanum and lets you add your dots in the Rote's Skill to the roll); exceeding the amount those things give you for free applies the number of Paradox dice determined by your Gnosis for every point you go over.<br /> <br /> In addition to Rotes, there are now also Praxes (singular Praxis), which are essentially a mage's signature spells \u2014 they share the Mana cost-break that Rotes have for non-Ruling Arcana and get an exceptional success on three successes, which allows the caster to gain benefits like regaining Willpower and Mana, ignoring Withstand ratings, or applying Conditions that give you Arcane Beats when resolved. They're also tied into how Legacies work, somewhat.<br /> <br /> Withstand ratings are Mage's answer to the problem of spellcasting not engaging with the normal rules for resisted or contested actions \u2014 a single success applies all of a spell's Potency to its effect and keeps doing so as long as it lasts, so greater resistance is handled by ratings that lower the effective Potency of a spell on a given target. So a mind-control spell has to have Potency higher than a target's Resolve to affect them, and sympathetic magic needs to be more powerful to use weaker connections to affect a target.<br /> <br /> Spellcasting aids like tools and runes and concentration and Demesnes have been generally collapsed into discrete categories and explicitly locked to spells and rituals for which their symbolism makes sense \u2014 a machine shop will help you reassemble or deconstruct things, but it won't do you much good for spells to scry on a rival unless you do the thematic legwork to connect those things.<br /> <br /> Your Nimbus and Shadow Name now have explicit story purposes that give you a reason to maintain your mundane and magical identities as separately as you can \u2014 casting magic while not Being A Wizard risks contaminating your nonmagical life with supernatural phenomena instead of limiting those things to aspects of your life as a mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T01:02:03-08:00","id":1027489,"title":"","content":"^ Like written before - Mage 1E and 2E are ( mechanically ) completely different games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:21:04-08:00","id":1027582,"title":"","content":"Mages also finally have a reason to act like Mages, and not like psychics. In 1st ED, things like chanting, using implements and other &quot;flavor&quot; choices didn't really give you anything; in fact, in a lot of situations they were a self-inflicted disadvantage that gave you nothing in return. Why cast a spell in a visible and noticeable way, if you could cast pretty much everything by standing perfectly still and just imagining it really hard?<br /> <br /> In 2nd ED, it's changed. Not because game forces you to do so, nothing so heavy handed. Basically, you need to sell your dice in exchange for power, and your basic dicepool is pitifully small. And how do you grab more dice? By including Yantras in your spellcasting - and Yantras are all this &quot;chanting&quot;, &quot;goat sacrificing&quot;, &quot;pointing a wand at&quot;, &quot;wearing rune-covered robes&quot; stuff. Without them, your spells won't unlock their true potential. <br /> Basically, game finally rewards you for Being A Wizard and Acting Like A Wizard, while also giving you freedom in defining what kind of wizard you are through use of Shadow Name. Hackier The Reality Hacker and Hermeticus The Hermetic are both viable concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:59:23-08:00","id":1027704,"title":"","content":"There have been a lot of updates to each of the specific gamelines but I think looking at the 2nd editions (or CofD vs nWoD as a whole) as separate entities from the 1st editions that needs to be moved from one end to the next is a sideways way of looking at the whole thing. <br /> <br /> It's not at all like going from cWoD to nWod (with the wording of the original post it sounds like this is how you're viewing it). It's more like a Software Patch to nWoD (with a different name due to licensing agreements between OP and WW). Each second edition is really just the first addition with some changes (the amount of which varies between gamelines). There are some major overhauls to be sure but the core of what makes CofD what it is is the same as the 1st Eds.<br /> <br /> Because of this picking things between the editions is (more or less) very easy as (for the most part) almost nothing is discarded in the 2nd Editions. They may not be included in the pages of the 2nd ed book but with those, the Devs have stated that they can still be in your games (though you may need to tweak them a little if you are using 2nd ed versions of those rules. Generally not super hard though).<br /> <br /> This ended up longer than I intended so I'll finish off with just stating that CofD remains how it has always been: A Toolbox for Players and Storytellers to dig into and pick what they want/need best for their own perfect individual awesome Stories to tell. So I wouldn't worry too much about having to &quot;discard&quot; 1st ed to replace it with 2nd ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T09:38:50-08:00","id":1027717,"title":"","content":"This thread might help you: <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?795923-Mage-The-Awakening-2nd-Edition-questions\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php...tion-questions</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T01:34:29-08:00","id":1028067,"title":"","content":"Another important change to 2nd Edition Awakening is that it further distances itself to Ascension mechanically by having Paradox be way less about Sleepers corroding spells and more about a Mage trying to use magic beyond what they're really capable of controlling. For instance Sleeper Paradox penalties is either +1 no matter the size of the gathering of Sleepers or maybe non-existent at all (would need to double check later), however if any Sleeper witnesses Supernal magic then they add the 9 again quality to the Paradox roll, if the gathering is I think ten or more it get's the 8 again quality, and a large gathering makes the Paradox roll gain the Rote quality. All of the dice bonuses to the Paradox roll now comes almost soley from a Mage not having Yantras they need on hand or by attempting to over Reach with their magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 01-07-2017, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}